## Full-colour illustration styles

- **Watercolour picture book** — soft edges, visible paper texture, muted palette. Classic, warm.
- **Flat vector** — bold flat shapes, no gradients, limited palette. Modern, very consistent across pages, forgiving of drift.
- **Textured digital painting** — painterly brushwork, rich lighting. Premium feel, hardest to keep consistent.
- **Gouache** — matte opaque colour, slightly chalky. Currently fashionable in trade picture books.
- **Cut-paper collage** — layered paper shapes with visible edges and shadow.
- **3D render / Pixar-adjacent** — volumetric lighting, soft subsurface skin. High appeal, high drift risk.
- **Crayon / child-art pastiche** — deliberately naive marks.

**Flat vector and cut-paper drift least** across a long book because they carry fewer variable details. Recommend them when the user is nervous about consistency or the book runs long.

