## Palette guidance

Fix a palette in the style descriptor and repeat it verbatim on every page. Name 4–6 colours explicitly rather than saying "warm palette", which the model interprets afresh each time.

- **Toddler**: high-saturation primaries and secondaries
- **Bedtime**: desaturated blues, dusty purples, cream, warm lamp yellow
- **Nature/seasonal**: sage, ochre, terracotta, cream, muted teal
- **Adult sophisticated**: limited 3-colour palette plus neutrals

---

## Style descriptor pattern

Compose one sentence, reused verbatim in every page prompt:

> `[style name], [line or brush quality], [palette], [rendering detail], [mood]`

Example: *"Clean cartoon outline coloring page, even 4pt black outlines with fully closed shapes, pure white background, no shading or grayscale, cheerful and friendly."*

Example: *"Soft watercolour picture-book illustration, visible cold-press paper texture, palette of sage green, cream, dusty rose, warm ochre and soft slate blue, gentle diffused afternoon light, cosy and calm."*
